<title>SPAIN: BBV issues $250 mln preferential shares.</title>
<headline>BBV issues $250 mln preferential shares.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Bilbao Vizcaya S.A. (BBV) said on Wednesday it had issued $250 million in preferential shares with a fixed dividend of eight percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The operation will be located in the North American retail market through the sale of American Depositary Receipts,&quot; BBV said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The issue will reinforce BBV's basic equity and the issue forms part of the strategy of actively administrating its capital, BBV said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
